  "title": "RBI Liquidity Mop-Up Auctions and India's Trade Deficit",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) received cumulative bids of ₹1.91 trillion against the ₹1.5 trillion liquidity mop-up target, indicating strong demand for liquidity amid surplus reserves. India's trade deficit widened to $31.98 billion in Q1FY27, partially offset by growth in exports of petroleum products, electronics, engineering, and marine goods.",
